<HTML><HEAD><META HTTP-EQUIV="Description" CONTENT="A discussion board for people who play druids in the game Everquest"><META HTTP-EQUIV="Keywords" CONTENT="message board, message boards, message board software, bulletin board, bulletin boards, forum, free forums, free message boards, eq, everquest, druids"><TITLE>LOL, I don't know about 34, but druids kick shaman *** before then. - www.ezboard.com</TITLE></HEAD><BODY TEXT=#333399 BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6 LINK=#990033 VLINK=#009966 ALINK=#FF6600 BACKGROUND=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/background.jpg><CENTER><CENTER><TABLE><TR><TD ALIGN=CENTER><A HREF=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/optinemail.html><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/images/email_banner1.gif border=0></A>&nbsp; <A HREF=http://www.ezboard.com><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/imgs/poweredby2.gif width=136 height=60 border=0></A>&nbsp; <A HREF="http://offers.getrelevant.com/OfferSelection.html?pwsID=111&chanID=83&ImgNum=1"><IMG SRC="http://images.getrelevant.com/p/111/83/1/49150" border="0" width=120 height=60></A><BR></TD></TR></TABLE></CENTER><BR><CENTER><A HREF=http://www.ezboard.com><IMG SRC=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/banners/noobiebeggers.gif BORDER=0></A><P></CENTER><TABLE WIDTH=95%><TR><TD><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>[ </FONT><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/bthedruidsgrove><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>The Druids Grove</FONT></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399> ]<BR><BR></FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;[ </FONT><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Class Balance Issues</FONT></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399> ] </FONT></TD><TD ALIGN=RIGHT><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showAddTopicScreenFromWeb><IMG SRC=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/newtopic.gif border=0></A>&nbsp; <A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=89.topic><IMG SRC=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/addreply.gif border=0></A></TD></TR></TABLE><table border=0 width=95% cellpadding=5 cellspacing=1><TR><TD valign=top><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>Author</FONT><B></TD><TD valign=top><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>Comment</FONT><B></FONT></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://server3.ezboard.com/bthedruidsgrove.showLocalUserPublicProfile?login=keldornstormreaper>Keldorn StormReaper</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/ezgfx/globalBlack.gif BORDER=0 HEIGHT=10 WIDTH=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Local user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>10/26/99</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>5:55:02 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>LOL, I don't know about 34, but druids kick shaman *** before then.</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>I've played a shaman to 20, a druid to 20. Shaman got to 20 in 7 days /played, fully twinked. Druid got to 20 in 3 days /played, UNTWINKED. Shamans can NEVER EVER THINK about taking on a camp solo. Druids do so with EASE. My damage shields have been known to have 10 to 1 damage to mana ratio. Shamans disease DoTs are a joke and Druid swarm line kicks their poison line. My druid gets BETTER buffs, that's right, I said BETTER buffs at low levels. Stat buffs at low levels are WORTHLESS. My druid would kick my shaman's ass out into space if they went head to head in a melee fight. Shamans can't compete with TPs so I'll skip that. Druid root works just as well for me as my shaman's roots and druids get snare as well. IMO, shamans clearly have worse DDs. They ONLY get cold DDs and not very of them at that. Druids get two DDs at every other spell level. Take it from someone who have played both shaman and druid, druids kick shaman ass until 34th level, when shamans get their pets. I am not sure about then but I am pretty sure about now.</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>trinsom</FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Unregistered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11/17/99</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>2:19:30 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>hmmmmm....</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Is this a cry of NERF me ?????</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Rhubarb</FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Unregistered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11/20/99</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>1:41:08 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Maybe correct until 24</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Druids certainly have an easier time up to level 24 (not 34), whereupon the balance is largely restored.  <BR>  <BR> This is primarily due to the poor spells given to shamen at 19 (and the comparatively decent spells given at 24), in addition to (as pointed out) buffs which are relatively less useful to lower levels (although importantly shamen do get SoW 5 levels earlier which goes a long way to addressing this). <BR>  <BR> When shamen later get pets, and druids get teleports, the two classes diverge beyond sensible comparison - its then a matter of style. <BR>  <BR> But at any level, any class played to its strengths will outdo any class not so played.</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Lyyo</FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Unregistered User</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>11/29/99</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>5:04:41 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Only to 20?   Askewed view</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>You are comparing spell power at early levels.  Sure i admit Druid have more spell power.  That's because they are caster heavy where as Shaman are melee heavy.   <BR>  <BR> Shaman get better armor at early levels, have bash, and have greater Str and HP. <BR>  <BR> Shaman DoTs actually do MORE damage per mana.  The only downside is that they take longer to do.  To compensate, they ALSO have many stackble DoTs.  When they are expected to finish most fights by melee, it makes complete sense to have drawn out DoT effects. <BR>  <BR> You also claim Druids have &quot;better&quot; buffs or DDs.  Druids only gain 20% more hp than the Shamen hp Buff and only do 20% more damage to its closely related Shamen DD spells.  When you realize that casting times are lower since the spell power is lower, it really doesnt mean you can outdamage by much. <BR>  <BR> Just so you know, Shamens also get a pet at the last level AND a DoT that does 1500 damage in 40 seconds.  They also get a spell that is almost like a haste effect for melee. <BR>  <BR> So why do i like my Druid over a Shamen then?  Exploration skills and group spells.  All my spells either help me round a group or help me explore a zone.  That's good enough for me *grins*. <BR>  <BR> Lyyo Windseer <BR> Level 45 Druid <BR> (The foraged stuff aint to eat, it's for getting lubricated)</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/ukemric.showPublicProfile>Kemric</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/ezgfx/gicons/black_bluespot.gif BORDER=0 HEIGHT=10 WIDTH=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Global user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>2/8/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>10:37:17 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT><BR><img src=http://users.demag.rwth-aachen.de/mustafa/guild/kemric.gif WIDTH=60 HEIGHT=60></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Re: Only to 20?   Askewed view</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>On a strictly Dueling basis: <BR>  <BR> I play both Druid(29) & Shaman(45), and I have watched many different duels, and participated in a few.  In the higher levels, there are few classes that can beat a shaman who is familiar with his abilities.  Of the duels I have personally witnessed, the only shaman 44 or higher I have seen get beat, was beaten by a Necro.  With two dots, a level 50 shaman can lay down 2500 points of damage(1600 in the first 40 sec).  That's for a bit over a bubble of mana.  At that point, the druid has a choice.  He has 40 seconds to either heal himself(do any 50 druids have 1600hp?), or nuke the shaman, and hope he dies in time so he can cure the dots on himself.  If the shaman has his pet, which double attacks for 51 dmg, there isn't really a contest.  Anything below 39 I would say could go either way in a duel, Druid, or Shaman, depending on the knowledge of the combatants.  After that i'd have to vote shaman. <BR>  <BR> Why do I play both? <BR>  <BR> Druids for teleporting, tracking, foraging, harmony, group buffs, and damage shields.  They have a wide variety of damage spells, from magic, to ice, to fire, to DOTS.  Playing a druid has been a breeze so far. <BR>  <BR> Shaman for the ability to tank better than any other priest/caster(how many casters can go face to face with an ice giant), the pets, slow down spells, speed up spells, and the best DOTS at many levels(especially 49).  Shamans are tough up until 24, where it gets a little easier.  Things start to get exponentially better at each circle starting at 34. <BR>  <BR> These aren't the only reasons, but these are the major benefits of those two classes.</FONT><P>Kemric Niata'Laodhan  45 Barbarian Shaman<BR>
Baldicus Hairytoes    29
Halfling Druid<BR>
Haneman Niata'Laodhan 22 Barbarian Warrior<BR>
Galdivan              21 HighElf Wizard<BR>
Reden                 11 Human Bard<BR>
<BR>
Clan Skallagrim - Mithaniel Marr<P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#f7f5e6><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/uozaak.showPublicProfile>Ozaak</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC= http://www.ezboard.com/ezgfx/gicons/misc_1.gif  BORDER=0 HEIGHT=10 WIDTH=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Global user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>2/8/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>3:52:40 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT><BR><img src=http://www.suvangi.com/~robj/x.gif><a href=http://www.suvangi.com/~robj/everquest/><img src=http://www.suvangi.com/~corayj/ozaak.GIF border=0><FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Re: LOL, I don't know about 34, but druids kick shaman *** before then.</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Shaman are the best class in the game for all around versitily, utility, and coolness.  So says me.</FONT><P><strong><font size=4 color="#333333"><u>Ozaak Kaazo                                        </u></font><br>
<font size=2 color="#660000">Not all Dwarves are bitter old men... some are dirty too.</font><br>
<font size=3 color="#664400">Bitter, dirty, old Dwarf.  Humble follower of Bristlebane</strong></font><br><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/bthedruidsgrove.showLocalUserPublicProfile?login=medicineman>Medicine Man</A></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Local user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>4/20/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>12:58:15 pm</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Re: LOL, I don't know about 34, but druids kick shaman *** before then.</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Druids just rock at soloing, specially when soloing outdoor mobs. The two spell lines I'd want would be the damage shield and harmony lines, great stuff.<br>
<br>
Shamans aren't as swift at taking groups of mobs, personally I've been able to take 2 low blues at level 28 but only on a rare occasion. I can take one mob out of a group but have to be ready to zone afterwards.<br>
<br>
It's all good though, I'm fine with my class' weaknesses and I'm content where I am.<br>
<br>
Cymrick Ravenfoot<br>
Shaman of Justice, Master of Recipies<br>
Wiseman of the 29th pillar<br>
<br>
CT</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE BORDER=0 WIDTH=95%><TR><TD ALIGN=LEFT></TD><TD ALIGN=RIGHT></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE WIDTH=95% BORDER=0><TR><TD><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.showAddReplyScreenFromWeb?topicID=89.topic&index=6><IMG SRC=http://www.execpc.com/~msippel/thedruidsgrove/images/addreply.gif border=0></A></TD><TD><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.emailToFriend?topicID=89.topic><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/images/email.gif BORDER=0 ALT="Email This To a Friend"></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>&nbsp;Email This To a Friend</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.threadControl?topicID=89.topic><IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/gfx/deleteThread.gif BORDER=0 ALT="Topic Control Image"></A><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>&nbsp;&nbsp;Topic Commands (Moderator only)</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.subscribeUnregisteredToTopic?topicID=89.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Subscribe</FONT></A>  <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Click to receive email notification of replies</FONT><BR><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/fthedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues.unsubscribeUnregisteredToTopic?topicID=89.topic><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Unsubscribe</FONT></A>  <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Click to stop receiving email notification of replies</FONT><BR></TD><TD></TD></TR><TR><TD COLSPAN=3 ALIGN=CENTER><BR><FORM ACTION=http://pub2.ezboard.com/BBSForum.jumpShowForum METHOD=POST><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Jump to: </FONT><SELECT NAME=forumName><OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovegeneral>General<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovekunark>Kunark<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovespells>Spells<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovequests>Quests<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovehuntingguide>Hunting Guide<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgrovedruidicequipment>Druidic Equipment<OPTION VALUE=thedruidsgroveclassbalanceissues>Class Balance Issues<OPTION V